{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"How do I resolve Amazon S3 AccessDenied errors in SageMaker AI training jobs?","context":"### Encrypted input bucket\n\nIf you encrypted data in the S3 bucket with AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS), then check the permissions. The IAM policy that's attached to the execution role must allow the **kms:encrypt** and **kms:decrypt** actions. Check that the AWS KMS key policy [grants access to the execution role](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policy-default.html#key-policy-default-allow-root-enable-iam).\n\nYou might use an AWS KMS key for the machine learning (ML) storage volume in the resource configuration of your job. If you use an AWS KMS key, then the IAM policy must allow the **kms:CreateGrant** action. For more information, see [Grants in AWS KMS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/grants.html).\n\n**Note:** It's a best practice to [encrypt the ML storage volume](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/encryption-at-rest-nbi.html).\n\nWhen you use the Python SDK and implement an abstraction of the **estimator.EstimatorBase** class, pass the **output\\_kms\\_key** and **volume\\_kms\\_key** parameters through **kwargs** keyword arguments. Take this action regardless of the documented presence of the **output\\_kms\\_key** and **volume\\_kms\\_key** parameters in the inheriting class. For more information, see [Estimators](https://sagemaker.readthedocs.io/en/v2.16.0/api/training/estimators.html) on the Amazon SageMaker Python SDK website","url":"https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/sagemaker-s3-accessdenied-training"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Encryption at rest for SageMaker AI Training Sessions","context":"##### Execution role\n\nThe IAM execution role you pass as `RoleArn` to\n`CreateTrainingSession` must have the following AWS KMS permissions.\nThese allow the training session to encrypt and decrypt your data through\nAmazon S3.\n\n```\n{\n \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n \"Statement\": [\n {\n \"Sid\": \"KMSPermissionsForS3Encryption\",\n \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n \"Action\": [\n \"kms:Decrypt\",\n \"kms:GenerateDataKey\"\n ],\n \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:kms:region:account-id:key/key-id\",\n \"Condition\": {\n \"StringLike\": {\n \"kms:ViaService\": \"s3.*.amazonaws.com\"\n }\n }\n }\n ]\n}\n```\n\nThe `kms:ViaService` condition (`s3.*.amazonaws.com`)\nrestricts the execution role use of the key to requests that come through Amazon S3.\nIf your bucket is configured with default encryption under a different KMS key,\nalso grant the execution role `kms:GenerateDataKey` and\n`kms:Decrypt` on that key so it can read and write objects in your\nbucket","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/training-sessions-encryption-at-rest.html"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Machine Learning Service – Amazon SageMaker FAQs – AWS","context":"#### What security measures does SageMaker AI have?\n\nSageMaker AI ensures that ML model artifacts and other system artifacts are encrypted in transit and at rest. Requests to the SageMaker AI API and console are made over a secure (SSL) connection. You pass AWS Identity and Access Management roles to SageMaker AI to provide permissions to access resources on your behalf for training and deployment. You can use encrypted Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) buckets for model artifacts and data, as well as pass an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key to SageMaker AI notebooks, training jobs, and endpoints to encrypt the attached ML storage volume. SageMaker AI also supports Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (Amazon VPC) and AWS PrivateLink support","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/ai/faqs/"}]}}

## Recent AWS announcements (What's New)

Newer than your training data may be. When these conflict with the documentation results above or with what you remember, prefer the most recent dated source.

{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"aws-ai-ml","skill_description":"Selects, deploys, and customizes AI models on Amazon SageMaker. Training or Processing jobs, fine-tuning (SFT/DPO/RLVR/RLAIF), model selection, evaluation, SageMaker or Bedrock deployment, inference optimization and endpoint diagnostics. Use when fine-tuning models on SageMaker, choosing a base model to customize or deploy from SageMaker JumpStart or Hub, SageMakerPublicHub, or the model catalog, checking data quality (duplicates, languages, PII), transforming or validating data (reformat, clean, filter, dedupe, split, merge, redact), generating synthetic data, labeling data with a model, human review or annotation and applying its corrections, evaluating model quality, deploying or optimizing endpoints, configuring IAM/S3, or managing SageMaker Managed MLflow. Use for endpoint health, latency, logs, metrics, errors. Covers Serverless Model Customization, Nova and OSS deployment paths, and PySDK v3. NOT for SageMaker Ground Truth labeling jobs, Feature Store, or general AWS infrastructure.\n\nServices: sagemaker, s3, iam, bedrock\nTasks: build, deploy, debug, optimize\nPersona: developer, data-scientist\nWorkload: ai-ml","skill_name":"aws-ai-ml"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"securing-s3-buckets","skill_description":"Create and secure S3 buckets following AWS best practices for access control, encryption, monitoring, and remediation of misconfigurations. Use when the user wants to secure a new bucket, audit an existing bucket, fix a security finding, configure encryption, or enable logging and monitoring. Do NOT use for general S3 data operations, S3 Tables setup, or discovering existing data assets.\n\n\nServices: s3, kms, cloudtrail, guardduty, config, accessanalyzer\nTasks: secure, audit, remediate, encrypt, monitor\nPersona: developer, security-engineer\nWorkload: storage, compliance\n*","skill_name":"securing-s3-buckets"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"creating-secrets-using-best-practices","skill_description":"Creates and manages secrets in AWS Secrets Manager following security best practices. Always use this skill when creating secrets — it sets up dedicated KMS encryption keys, automatic rotation, least-privilege IAM policies, CloudTrail auditing, and lifecycle management that are essential for production-grade secret handling.\n\nServices: secrets-manager, kms, iam, cloudtrail, cloudwatch, lambda\nTasks: create, secure, configure\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: security\n*","skill_name":"creating-secrets-using-best-practices"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Verify SageMaker execution role KMS and S3 permissions"}
